      "rev_n_1_6be600_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_1_6be600_0",
        "node_id": "n_1_6be600",
        "thought_text": "Start by identifying all asterisks '*' in the grid. For each asterisk, attempt to place a star centered at that position with the largest possible size such that the entire star remains within the grid boundaries. Continue this process until all asterisks are covered or determine if it's impossible.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794391086.810077
      },
      "rev_n_2_9879f3_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_2_9879f3_0",
        "node_id": "n_2_9879f3",
        "thought_text": "Iterate through each cell in the grid. If a cell contains an asterisk '*', check if placing a star of size 1 centered at that cell would cover the asterisk. If so, mark the surrounding cells as covered. Repeat this process, incrementing the star size, until all asterisks are covered or determine impossibility.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794391086.810095
      },
      "rev_n_3_3c9c40_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_3c9c40_0",
        "node_id": "n_3_3c9c40",
        "thought_text": "Use a greedy approach to place stars. Start with the largest possible star size that fits within the grid and attempt to place it in every possible position. If a star can be placed without overlapping with previously placed stars, mark the cells as covered. Continue with smaller star sizes until all asterisks are covered or determine impossibility.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794391086.810105
      },
      "rev_n_4_9304fd_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_4_9304fd_0",
        "node_id": "n_4_9304fd",
        "thought_text": "Iterate through each cell in the grid and attempt to place the largest possible star centered at each asterisk. Track which cells are covered by stars to ensure all asterisks are covered without overlapping.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5966115425937684956",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794391164.4969568
      },
      "rev_n_5_441c6b_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_5_441c6b_0",
        "node_id": "n_5_441c6b",
        "thought_text": "Start by placing stars centered at asterisks with the smallest possible size that cover their respective positions. Gradually increase the size of these stars to cover adjacent asterisks, ensuring no conflicts arise.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5966115425937684956",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794391164.496969
      },
      "rev_n_6_d1202a_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_6_d1202a_0",
        "node_id": "n_6_d1202a",
        "thought_text": "Use a greedy approach to place stars, starting with the largest possible size at each asterisk. If a conflict arises, reduce the size of the star and try again. This ensures that the maximum number of asterisks are covered efficiently.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5966115425937684956",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794391164.4969752
      },
      "rev_n_7_c03c65_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_7_c03c65_0",
        "node_id": "n_7_c03c65",
        "thought_text": "Iterate through each cell in the grid. For each asterisk '*', attempt to place the smallest possible star centered on that cell that covers the asterisk without overlapping another asterisk. Continue this process until all asterisks are covered or determine impossibility.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "939880114394067957",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794391208.682014
      },
      "rev_n_8_eae368_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_8_eae368_0",
        "node_id": "n_8_eae368",
        "thought_text": "Preprocess the grid to identify clusters of asterisks. For each cluster, determine the minimum star size required to cover the entire cluster. Place stars of appropriate sizes to cover each cluster without overlap.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "939880114394067957",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794391208.6820521
      },
      "rev_n_9_0ec5ed_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_9_0ec5ed_0",
        "node_id": "n_9_0ec5ed",
        "thought_text": "Use a greedy algorithm starting from the largest possible stars and working downwards. Attempt to place the largest star that fits in the grid and covers an asterisk, marking the cells as covered. Continue with smaller stars until all asterisks are covered or determine impossibility.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "939880114394067957",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794391208.6820679
      },
      "rev_n_10_be465a_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_10_be465a_0",
        "node_id": "n_10_be465a",
        "thought_text": "Consider using a backtracking approach to try placing stars of different sizes in various positions. If placing a star of a certain size fails, backtrack and try a different configuration. This could potentially find a solution that a greedy approach might miss.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-8432554519692687394",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794391249.923174
      },
      "rev_n_11_2da93d_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_11_2da93d_0",
        "node_id": "n_11_2da93d",
        "thought_text": "Instead of starting with the largest star size, try placing stars of smaller sizes first. This might allow for more flexibility in covering the grid, especially in areas where larger stars cannot fit due to constraints.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-8432554519692687394",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794391249.9232209
      },
      "rev_n_12_0824ef_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_12_0824ef_0",
        "node_id": "n_12_0824ef",
        "thought_text": "Analyze the grid to identify patterns or clusters of asterisks that can be efficiently covered by a single star. Focus on covering these clusters first before attempting to cover individual asterisks, which could reduce the total number of stars needed.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-8432554519692687394",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794391249.923237
      },
      "rev_n_13_18c98c_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_13_18c98c_0",
        "node_id": "n_13_18c98c",
        "thought_text": "The current approach of trying to cover each asterisk individually might lead to inefficient solutions. Instead, we could try to group asterisks that can be covered by a single star of larger size, reducing the total number of stars needed.",
